<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Token Radar B — pre-token protocols, ranked by implied launch value</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css">
<script src="../data.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<header class="masthead">
  <p class="eyebrow">Token Radar · Route B — a second look at the same snapshot</p>
  <h1>Which pre-token protocol is worth farming next?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every protocol below <strong>records no token</strong> in the snapshot — that is the
  record, not proof it has none. Each is ranked by what its launch would be worth if its record
  stayed as it is, with the five steps to farm it. Implied values are this board's own claim,
  never a prediction that a token will launch, or when.</p>
  <dl class="stats" id="stats"></dl>
</header>

<main>
  <details class="method" id="method">
    <summary>How the value is worked out — the whole model, in the open</summary>
    <p><code>implied = TVL × category multiple × momentum × seasoning × breadth × credibility</code></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Category multiple.</strong> The median market-cap / TVL of the token-having protocols in the
      same category, shrunk toward the snapshot's global median when a category has few peers, then clamped
      to 0.05–0.80. No name is ever hard-coded: the multiples come from this snapshot's own figures.</li>
      <li><strong>Momentum.</strong> 1 + 0.4 × the 7-day TVL change, winsorised to −40%…+60%. A spike above
      +60% is capped and flagged — check it is not mercenary capital before you trust it.</li>
      <li><strong>Seasoning.</strong> 0.75 + 0.25 × age / 3 years. Older protocols with no token yet have
      survived longer without one; unknown age takes the 0.75 floor.</li>
      <li><strong>Breadth.</strong> +2% per extra chain, at most +8%.</li>
      <li><strong>Credibility.</strong> Starts at 1.00 and loses 0.03 for a missing 7-day change, 0.03 for a
      missing listing date, 0.02 for TVL under $10M, 0.02 for a single chain (floor 0.90). Thin or
      incomplete records are penalised, never rewarded — and nobody is dropped from the board for them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Two lenses: <strong>Implied value</strong> ranks by the model above; <strong>Early movers</strong>
    ranks by momentum × youth, the protocols moving fastest while still young. The board covers all 40
    watchlist protocols plus 158 more below the $50M floor.</p>
    <div id="multiples"></div>
  </details>

  <section class="controls" aria-label="Filter and sort">
    <label>Search <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="protocol name or slug…" autocomplete="off"></label>
    <label>Category <select id="cat"><option value="">All categories</option></select></label>
    <label>Min TVL <select id="minTvl">
      <option value="0" selected>Any TVL</option>
      <option value="10000000">$10M+</option>
      <option value="50000000">$50M+</option>
      <option value="100000000">$100M+</option>
      <option value="1000000000">$1B+</option>
    </select></label>
    <label class="check"><input id="watchOnly" type="checkbox"> Watchlist only</label>
    <label>Lens <select id="lens">
      <option value="implied">Implied value</option>
      <option value="early">Early movers</option>
    </select></label>
    <label>Sort <select id="sort">
      <option value="implied">Implied value ↓</option>
      <option value="tvl">TVL ↓</option>
      <option value="growth">7-day change ↓</option>
      <option value="age">Age ↓</option>
    </select></label>
  </section>

  <p class="count" id="count"></p>

  <section class="detail" id="detail" hidden></section>

  <table class="board">
    <thead><tr>
      <th>#</th><th>Protocol</th><th>Category</th><th>Chains</th>
      <th class="num">TVL</th><th class="num">7d</th><th class="num">Age</th>
      <th class="num">Implied value</th><th class="num" id="lensHead">Share</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="more" id="more"></p>
</main>

<footer>
  <p>Snapshot: DefiLlama protocol data fetched 2026-11-14, 758 protocols at or above $5M TVL, floor $50M.
  “Records no token” means the snapshot carries no gecko_id, symbol or market cap for it. A protocol on
  this board may still have a token its record does not carry. Farm steps are this board's plan, not
  financial advice; never risk money you cannot afford to lose.</p>
  <p>Judge's note: this entry is Route B. Its model is category-relative multiples with shrinkage, not a
  flat TVL multiple; its farm plans run on a weekly cadence with a stated cost and time per step; and its
  credibility factor docks thin records instead of trusting them. Every factor above is computed from the
  snapshot at run time — see <code>lib/model.ts</code>, functions <code>categoryMultiples</code>,
  <code>scoreProtocol</code> and <code>farmPlan</code>.</p>
</footer>
<script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```
